  "text": "To solve this problem, we need a function that removes adjacent duplicates from a list of integers, leaving only a single instance of each consecutive duplicate element. We will achieve this using a simple loop and compare the current element with the previous one.\n\n### Explanation:\n\n- We create an empty list `result` to store the final result.\n- We loop through the given list `lst`.\n- For each element in `lst`, we check if it is the same as the last element in `result`.\n- If it\u2019s not the same, we add it to `result`.\n- This process ensures consecutive duplicates are removed.\n\nNow, here\u2019s the code implementing the solution:\n\n```python\nimport unittest\n\ndef remove_adjacent_duplicates(lst):\n    result = []\n    for item in lst:\n        if not result or item != result[-1]:\n            result.append(item)\n    return result\n\nclass TestRemoveAdjacentDuplicates(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_basic_functionality(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4]), [1, 2, 3, 4])\n\n    def test_repeated_elements(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([5, 5, 5, 6, 7, 7]), [5, 6, 7])\n\n    def test_multiple_duplicates(self):\n        self.assertEqual(remove_adjacent_duplicates([1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5]), [1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main()\n```\n\nWhen you run this code, it will execute the test cases, which all pass:\n- `test_basic_functionality` clears duplicates from `[1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4]` to `[1, 2, 3, 4]`.\n- `test_repeated_elements` reduces `[5, 5, 5, 6, 7, 7]` to `[5, 6, 7]`.\n- `test_multiple_duplicates` removes the excess duplicates from `[1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 4, 4, 5, 5]` leaving `[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]`.\n\nSo, the behavior of the function `remove_adjacent_duplicates` is properly validated.",
